Note on PyQt5: it is offered under GPL v3 or a commercial licence from
Riverbank Computing. Distributing a binary of Quenchkey that bundles PyQt5
therefore places the combined work under the GPL unless you hold a commercial
Riverbank licence. Apache 2.0 on this source code does not change that, and it
is a constraint on distribution rather than on use. If that matters to you, the
interface layer is confined to quenchkey/ui/ and the core has no Qt dependency
at all — quenchkey/{crypto,vault,locker,archive,expiry,chain,certificate,
recovery,factors,passphrase,keyfile}.py import nothing from PyQt5, and
tools/quenchkey-recover.py needs neither Qt nor this package.
